    "body": "## Outcome\n\nThis completes the retained GI-0 foundation in #958, resets the repository around the active geometric-intelligence programme, and makes the existing geometric router approachable without sending a newcomer into the historical multi-hour model compiler.\n\n### Foundation retained from #958\n\n- source-free fixed-zeta prime-route algebra and a canonical schema-2 spin manifest;\n- prime atoms, semiprime experts including `p^2` self-loops, ordered n-lets, spin/torsion state, Hopf projection, golden radial shells, typed null/identity and trigonometric chart transitions;\n- bounded recursive geometric candidate mechanics and matched controls;\n- exact source-free SpiralCore operator fixtures and the optional six-prime chart; and\n- byte-identical one-worker/four-worker artifacts with 32/32 exact matches and a measured 1.484x compile-stage speedup on the frozen bounded canary.\n\nThe terminal capability boundary remains `RETAIN_STORAGE_RECALL_ONLY`. This does not establish recursive product attention, source-free coherent generation, real geometric chat, correctness, reasoning, frontier-like capability, or energy superiority.\n\n### New project front door\n\n- Replaced the 406-line historical README with an approximately 150-line reader-first explanation of the real goal, honest current state, shortest interaction path, and active programme.\n- Reduced `docs/README.md` to a current-authority map and a separate research archive.\n- Bare `r4`, `cargo run --bin r4 -- demo`, `./uor-r4-cli`, and `./r4-app.sh` now launch the bounded no-model geometric research dashboard.\n- `cargo run --bin r4 -- route \"geometry is the route\"` returns one inspectable geometric route without loading weights.\n- `just wasm-dashboard` is the explicit browser-only WASM build/serve path.\n- The legacy multi-stage model orchestrator is available only through `./uor-r4-cli --legacy-model-orchestrator`.\n- The dashboard defaults to geometric routing, rejects stale R4G1 defaults in demo mode, and puts teacher/R4G1 controls behind an explicitly historical section.\n- Native and WASM demo interactions return route telemetry and nearest indexed material marked `route-only-research-demo` and `not_an_answer`; they do not pass pathological geometric continuations off as intelligence.\n\n### Repository policy and the immutable ruleset\n\nReal development QA remains dormant and manual. The scheduled Kani run is now dormant as well.\n\nRepository ruleset `19597522` cannot be changed with the available write-level permission and still requires five historical status names plus a squash merge queue. To allow normal contributors to merge without reviving obsolete QA, pull-request and merge-group events now emit five instantaneous **transport acknowledgements** under those exact names. Each job performs no checkout, build, test, lint, audit, fuzz, WASM build, model evaluation, or certification. They are explicitly not PASS evidence. The forced queue is transport only; no admin bypass is used. #940 now represents eventual cleanup rather than a blocker.\n\n## Current programme\n\n`docs/geometric_intelligence_programme.md` is authoritative. The live sequence is `#961 -> #952 -> #953 -> #954 -> #955 -> #962 -> #963 -> #964 -> #965`: reversible lexical geometry, complete recursive attention, source-free grammatical inference, correctness and abstention, reasoning, product integration, measured optimization, serving-contract closure, then release QA.\n\n## Verification performed\n\nNo workspace test, BDD suite, doctest, no_std ladder, audit, fuzz run, Gate C run, corpus compile, model evaluation, or WASM build was run.\n\nTwo bounded product interactions were performed because this PR changes the user-facing entry point:\n\n1. `cargo run --bin r4 -- route \"geometry is the route\"` compiled the touched native product in 37.86 seconds and returned a real W7 route, kappa, deficit angle, Hopf state, UOR address, and nearest indexed route.\n2. The native `r4 demo` HTTP surface returned `research_demo: true`, then `/api/chat` returned `route-only-research-demo`, `not_an_answer: true`, W7 telemetry, and nearest indexed material. A remaining historical startup lock was found during this interaction, removed from demo mode, and the clean interaction was repeated successfully.\n\nThe standalone WASM build remains `NOT_RUN`; the existing Pages deployment workflow owns that product build after merge.\n\nCloses #958\n",
